    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "A noncentral $ \\chi^{2} $ arises when the random variables being considered have nonzero means. In particular, if $ x_{i} \\sim \\mathrm{N}(\\mu_{i}, 1) $, then $ u = \\sum_{i=1}^{n} x_{i}^{2} $ follows a noncentral $ \\chi^{2} $ distribution with n degrees of freedom and noncentrality parameter",
      "source_page": 890,
      "printed_page": 870,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_appendix1:p072:b17"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        150.0,
